# 5 entries, one genuinely distinct fact per line.
kumain | definition | Kumain means to eat, and it is the ordinary Tagalog verb used at the table, in the kitchen and when talking about a meal. Its forms are the ones a learner meets first: kumain for the completed or general, kumakain for the ongoing, and kakain for the future, all built on the root kain with different affixes rather than being separate words. The polite form adds a prefix, so kumain ka means please eat, and it is the form used to a guest or to someone older. A related verb is inumin for to drink, and the pair is a common learner confusion because English separates eating and drinking while many Filipino sentences use kumain more loosely for both. The noun pagkain means food in general, so pagkaon and pagkain are close variants and both are correct depending on region, with pagkain the more common form in Manila. | eat, food, meal, drink, hungry, verb tense | anong meaning ng kumain, kumain meaning, paano magngumana ng kumain | kain | kain
